course: dictionary
lesson: 5151
title: Ironclad: armour and certainty
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ironclad has a clear picture inside it: iron, like a suit of armour. The word is made of two parts, iron and clad, and clad means covered. So an ironclad thing is covered in iron, or protected as if it were.
explain: Context shows you which meaning is used. «The diabolical ironclad beetle of the USA has armour that scientists found could take a force about 39,000 times its weight.» The words armour and force tell you the beetle is protected by a hard covering, so ironclad means covered in strong armour.
explain: Ironclad can also be used for promises and excuses. «I have an ironclad alibi» means the proof is so strong that nobody can break it. When you meet ironclad, ask yourself: is this about metal armour, or about being very sure?
fact: Ironclad means covered or protected with iron plates.
fact: An ironclad was a warship from the 1800s, covered with iron armour.
fact: The USS Monitor and the CSS Virginia were ironclad ships, and they fought in 1862.
fact: «Ironclad» can mean so strong it cannot be broken or doubted: an ironclad guarantee, alibi or excuse.
exercise: «The diabolical ironclad beetle of the USA has armour that scientists found could take a force about 39,000 times its weight.» What does ironclad mean in this sentence? | *Covered in hard, strong armour | Able to fly very fast | Painted bright green | Small and soft
exercise: In 1862 the USS Monitor fought the CSS Virginia. What was an ironclad? | A type of small bird | A sailing boat with bright sails | A loud drum played in a band | *A warship covered with iron armour
exercise: Dad says, «I have an ironclad alibi, so nobody can blame me.» What does ironclad suggest here? | *Very sure, so it cannot be broken | Made of old wood | Easy to break | Slightly sad
test: «Our club gave an ironclad guarantee that the trip would be safe.» What does ironclad mean here? | Made of iron, like a ship | *Very sure, so it cannot be doubted | Slightly late | Quite small
test: Which thing is an ironclad? | A tin of paint | A promise that nobody can break | A soft cloud in the sky | *A warship with iron armour
exam: Which meaning fits «ironclad ship» best? | A ship that sinks very fast | A ship full of food | A ship painted white | *A ship covered with iron armour
